    <string name="boss_intro_1">The Old Mallard. Three good photos fill its album. After each page it ducks out of sight for a moment, and on the last page it pretends to fly off before coming back.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_2">The Twin Teals. Two of them fly at once and either one fills a page, but they swap places as soon as one is photographed.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_3">The Wind Goose. It glides with the gusts, which push it sideways. For the last page it leads a flock: aim at the leader.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_4">The Mist Goose. It only shows itself between the fog banks, and less and less with every page. Wait for it to come out.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_5">The Thief Crow. If your album does not grow for three seconds, it steals a page back. Keep shooting.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_6">The Royal Snow Goose. It melts into the snow every few seconds, and you must wind the roll after each photo.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_7">The Royal Grebe. It dives and surfaces where you least expect it, farther away every time. Watch the rings on the water.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_8">The Imperial Mandarin. It hops from tree to tree and rests a moment on each perch: that is your chance.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_9">The Ghost Duck. You can barely see it, but it glows just before it changes course. Shoot when it shines.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_10">The Thunder Flock. A V of geese: a photo with at least three of them fills a page. Lightning breaks the V for a moment.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_11">The Golden Eider. It loops around the whole field, and every good photo in a row raises the multiplier.</string>
    <string name="boss_intro_12">The Great Duck. One page in the mist, one as a ghost and the last one diving. Everything you learned, together.</string>
    <string name="boss_stole">The crow stole a page!</string>
